{
  "slug": "shepherd",
  "name": "Shepherd",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Shepherd tracks, preserves, and auto-cleans the background processes Claude Code's Bash tool leaves running dev servers, build watchers, test runners. Each Claude session gets its own tracked list, so you can stash a dev server to free RAM, bring it back later in the same working directory, kill just one session's processes without touching another's, and when Claude crashes have its orphaned children cleaned up automatically on the next launch.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **9 commands** and **5 hooks**.\n\n- **Commands** (9): `adopt` (Register an externally-spawned pid as tracked in the current session (processes from a previous Claude, from another terminal,…), `cleanup` (Kill tracked processes older than a duration or using more than a RAM size), `kill` (Terminate tracked background processes), `processes` (List background processes Claude has spawned across all tracked sessions), `rm` (Delete a stashed snapshot without resuming it), `stash` (Snapshot + kill this session's background processes to free RAM), `stashes` (Show all saved stash snapshots with their command, cwd, and timestamp), `status` (One-line summary of tracked Claude sessions, processes, and orphans), and 1 more\n- **Hooks** (5): `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install shepherd@claude-community` from `mgorkemuz/claude-code-shepherd`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "hook": 5,
    "command": 9
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "gorkemuz"
  },
